#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:23
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:25
msgid "If you are experiencing an issue with OpenShot, such as a freeze, crash, or error message, there are many different techniques which can be useful for troubleshooting the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:31
msgid "Large or Slow Project Files with Audio Waveforms"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:33
msgid "Older projects with many audio waveforms can have unusually large ``.osp`` files and take longer to open or save. Older builds stored the waveform measurements inside the project file, sometimes repeating them for clips and undo history."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:37
msgid "The latest build stores these measurements in **separate compressed waveform files** instead. The project keeps small references to those files, reducing the data copied during editing and written into the ``.osp`` file. These files describe audio levels for display, not copies of the audio itself; your media and exported sound are unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:43
msgid "To update an older project:"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:45
msgid "Open it in the latest build. OpenShot automatically moves embedded waveform data into its waveform cache, preserving the existing waveform appearance."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:47
msgid "Choose :guilabel:`File → Save Project As` to keep the original project as a backup, or save normally to update the existing file."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:49
msgid "Keep the saved project's ``_assets`` folder alongside its ``.osp`` file when copying or backing up the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:52
msgid "For example, ``MyProject.osp`` stores its compressed ``.wfc`` waveform files in ``MyProject_assets/waveforms/``. Each file contains compact numeric measurements compressed for storage. Identical waveform data can share the same cache file. OpenShot also uses a local cache while you work, including before the first save."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:57
msgid "The first opening still needs to read the old embedded data, so it can take time. The smaller project file is written when you save. Generating a waveform for a new, long audio file still requires analyzing that audio. If waveform cache files are missing, OpenShot can rebuild visible waveforms from the original media. See :ref:`timeline_waveform_display_ref` for waveform display and regeneration options."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:66
msgid "Using Logs to Troubleshoot a Problem"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:68
msgid "A log is a text file that records what OpenShot is doing, along with warnings and errors. These files can help the support team understand a problem, even when you do not see an error message on screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:72
msgid "OpenShot keeps two log files in the ``.openshot_qt`` folder inside your home folder. On Linux and macOS, this location is written as ``~/.openshot_qt/``. The folder may be hidden in your file manager."
msgstr ""

