#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:350
msgid "High DPI / 4K Monitors"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:352
msgid "OpenShot Video Editor provides robust support for High DPI (Dots Per Inch) monitors, ensuring that the interface looks sharp and is easily readable on displays with various DPI settings. This support is particularly helpful on 4K monitors and other high-resolution displays."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:358
msgid "Per Monitor DPI Awareness"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:360
msgid "OpenShot is DPI aware on a per-monitor basis, meaning it can adjust its scaling dynamically depending on the DPI settings of each connected monitor. This helps provide a consistent experience across different displays."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:365
msgid "DPI Scaling on Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:367
msgid "On Windows, OpenShot rounds the scaling factor to the nearest whole value to maintain visual integrity. This helps avoid visual artifacts in the UI and keeps interface elements crisp and well-aligned. Due to this rounding, some scaling options can lead to larger fonts and UI elements than expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:372
msgid "**125% scaling** rounds to **100%**"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:373
msgid "**150% scaling** rounds to **200%**"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:376
msgid "Workarounds for Fine-Grained Adjustment"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:378
msgid "While rounding helps maintain a clean interface, there are workarounds for users who require more precise control over scaling. These methods are **not recommended** due to potential visual artifacts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:382
msgid "**QT_SCALE_FACTOR_ROUNDING_POLICY=PassThrough**"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:384
msgid "Setting this environment variable can disable rounding and allow more precise scaling."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:385
msgid "**Note:** This may cause visual artifacts, particularly in the timeline, and is not recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:387
msgid "**QT_SCALE_FACTOR=1.25** (or similar value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:389
msgid "Manually setting the scale factor can provide finer adjustments to the font and UI scaling."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:390
msgid "This can also be set via Preferences (User Interface Scale), but expect border/line issues on Windows with fractional scales."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:391
msgid "**Note:** This method can also lead to visual artifacts and make OpenShot harder to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/troubleshoot.rst:393
msgid "For more info on adjusting these environment variables, please visit https://github.com/OpenShot/openshot-qt/wiki/OpenShot-UI-too-large."
msgstr ""
